      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/o8kqVa66gBJtEkqVmhxQO2qwDIA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/256978-chef-johns-cuban-sandwich-step-2-BP-2635-6e888cbf790e4c7d8f4e96ebc5fae6fa.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/256968/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Trim off ends of bread. Cut loaf in half and evenly split bread to make tops and bottoms of two sandwiches.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/47IgAvIUv7vJBTy1XGdGzfrcv5Q=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/256978-chef-johns-cuban-sandwich-step-3-BP-2642-4f5965cab60e42ae83019a00a5b1f249.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/256968/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spread each half on both sides generously with mayo-mustard sauce.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/IDduquBKZ2iVm16ooH1E34nE5sE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/256978-chef-johns-cuban-sandwich-step-4-BP-2647-26e6b2ebd1d34af8a33df876c524388c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/256968/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide sandwich ingredients between the two bottom halves in this order: 2 slices Swiss cheese, 3 slices ham, hot cooked pork, pickle slices, and 2 more slices Swiss cheese. Place tops on sandwiches.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/BEQADhWpZHdrvyz5lNT4YlpUowg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/256978-chef-johns-cuban-sandwich-step-5-BP-2656-99014c927c93470487035a52ca58fec4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/256968/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt butter in a heavy skillet over medium heat. Place sandwiches in the skillet and press down with a heavy weight, such as another skillet or foil-wrapped bricks. Toast sandwiches until bread is crisp and filling is heated through, 3 or 4 minutes per side.",
